WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.702
-I´m so happy to have you here.
-I´m so happy to be here.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
It´s my first talk show ever.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s your first talk show.
-Yes.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m so honored
to have you here.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.375 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we --
Before you were a cast member,

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.946
we wrote together at "SNL."

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to make sure I have
my timeline right,

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.751
because then you wrote and
performed on the "Maya &amp; Marty"

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
variety special...
-Yep.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.587
...before you were a cast member
at "SNL?"

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Correct, yeah.
-And how was your time working

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Maya and Marty short?
-It was fantastic.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those two are amazing.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Martin Short would
totally mess with me.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He likes to take people down,
in a fun way.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He really does.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.636
-We would be shooting sketches,

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there would be
a studio audience.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then during stop downs,
it was kind of quiet

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.010
and the studio audience were
just kind of looking at us.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.479
And he´d be like, "Mikey, tell
everyone what it´s like to be

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.448
the least famous person here."

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s just kind
of like that dude.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But he´s so endearing.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
He´s very charming.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was fantastic.
-So, you wrote --

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as somebody
who wrote on the show,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.560
I have inherent jealousy
when someone writes a hit.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.963
Because David S. Pumpkins was
an immediate hit of a sketch.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was very fun.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.234 size:75% position:38%
-It was interesting.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tom Hanks is amazing.
-Yeah.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
This sketch is so popular,
not only did it explode

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.040
as a Halloween costume --

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a Madam Tussaud´s
David S. Pumpkins.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.977
-Yeah, and that´s fantastic.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:22.048
What´s awesome about this is you
can tell they just put

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:25.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
a David Pumpkins suit
on an existing Tom Hanks...

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:28.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you´re right.
-...because he´s so calm.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.191
And I think this is in the room
that was, like,

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Hollywood party.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because it´s just clearly
Tom Hanks, like, "Hi."

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.696 size:81% position:41%
-I´m so mad at myself
that I did not realize

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.131 size:78% position:39%
that´s what they did.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can´t believe how quickly
they made a new wax Tom Hanks.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, right?
Let´s make David Pumpkins

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
just chilling with
a nice smile on his face.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.208
-So, now you have an animated
David S. Pumpkins special.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-You are one of the voices.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
You co-wrote it.
-Yeah, with Bobby Moynihan

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Streeter Seidell.
-This is animated special.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-It looks a little bit --

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s got, like, some Saturday
morning cartoon graphics.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:02:02.322
-It´s got a very old-school kind
of throwback animation style.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For kids?
-Is it kid-friendly?

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
That´s how it came to be.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
We -- Especially
after the sketch, like,

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.831
seeing social media and
a lot of kids dressing up

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:15.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
as David Pumpkins.
I saw YouTube videos of kids

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.538 size:81% position:41%
acting out the sketch
from beginning to end.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:23.109
And we thought it would be fun
to do a Halloween special, like,

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.178
with David Pumpkins for kids.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:29.015
Because David pumpkins is
kind of like a kid himself.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, this thing
is very like --

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
My 5-year-old son does
that type of thing,

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:37.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we decided to gear
it towards kids.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.659 size:84% position:42%
And there´s a lot of --
There´s kind of like

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
a leaving cookies
for Santa Claus.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-There´s the David Pumpkins

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.767
equivalent, you know, for kids.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.370
-Now I do want to point out your
time-slot for your cartoon

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
for kids is 11:30
on Saturday night.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.176
Which is very David Pumpkins...
-Yes.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.978
-...because you have questions.
-You immediately have questions.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
It also might be

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:01.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was no room.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:05.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Lorne gave us
the first half hour of "SNL."

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
But --
-I feel like I´m going to

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
turn on
Saturday morning cartoons

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.622
and it´s going to be
like a Keith Morrison "Dateline"

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the grisliest
Halloween murders.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.259
And I´ll be like, "You guys
should have flipped these."

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This is in
the wrong time slot."

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So --
-Yeah -- you --

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.798 size:84% position:42%
Bobby Moynihan was here
and talked a little bit

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.066
about the origins of sketch.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
Originally --
And then we have

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.369
the Bobby cartoon and then
we have the you cartoon.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And he said himself, he said,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We should be left skeleton
and fat skeleton."

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-Like -- and I said,

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.845
"No, you´re right skeleton."

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You´ve been
a writer now since 2013.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of my favorite
things to ask --

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.286
sketches that you have pitched
that have not found their way

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the show.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are so many.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:48.962 size:81% position:41%
-There was one I wrote
with Streeter Seidell,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.464
who I wrote the David Pumpkins
sketch and the special with.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Great writer, as well.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.568
-We thought it was so funny.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:59.405
It was a commercial parody
for a car security system

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:03.743
that would guarantee that no
thief would break into your car.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-And it was a bag of

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:09.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
old McDonald´s on --
on the floor

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your passenger seat.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you could tell
by the audience.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, it was a huge hit...

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, sure.
-...at the table read.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m sure Lorne´s going
to watch that when he hears

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.592
that audience lose their mind.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my gosh!

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.296
It needs to go straight to air!"

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, we thought --
-So, was the idea

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:27.166
a criminal would see the bag --
-Yeah, it would, like --

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
It had testimonials
from car thieves and --

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:32.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they were like,
"Look, if I´m going

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:35.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
to break into a car and I see
a bag of old McDonald´s

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.144
on the floor, like, I know
it´s going to smell bad,

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.846
have that old McDonald´s smell."
-Yeah.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:44.284
"And there´s ten other cars on
this block that don´t smell."

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there was
a deluxe system

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
that had a leash and
a wet towel in the back seat.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:49.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And it was like --

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
like you took
your dog to the beach.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, there you go.
-And we --

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
Streeter and I were like,
"Oh, this is going to crush."

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then it was just nothing.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we´re like, "Okay,
we hate this now."

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s so funny how quickly --
-Uh, anything else?

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:06.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had a --
with Brian Tucker,

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had a sketch
of Mortal Kombat.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:13.746
It was a few years ago,
Mortal Kombat X was coming out.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And Pete was playing

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.550
a video game and it --
You know those character select

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.552 size:88% position:44%
screens where it´s like,
"Choose your fighter,"

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it´s like,
"Raiden. Scorpion."

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just --
And then it was like, "Raiden.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
Scorpion, Sonya."

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.559
And then it went to Kevin Hart.
-Uh-huh.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.562
-And he looked like Flavor Flav,
I would say.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:33.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just went,
[ High voice ] "Crazy cheese!"

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:34.867
[ Normal voice ]
And then Pete was like, "What?"

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, of course,
he did not want Crazy Cheese.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.507 size:88% position:44%
And it was like, "You´ve
selected Crazy Cheese."

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And then I just remember

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:48.014
his combo move was Leslie Jones
came out as his girlfriend

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.415 size:81% position:41%
and went, "I´m Karen!"

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was a little
too complicated.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe some day.
-Some day.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um -- uh.
-Yeah.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.692 size:88% position:44%
-Judging by the audience
response Mortal also --

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:02.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think --
"SNL" is back next week.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:04.564
I think we can look forward to
both McDonald´s security system

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Crazy Cheese.
-Yeah, it´s going to dominate

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
the show.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can´t wait to see the
special.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you very much
for being here, Mikey.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, I love you.
-It´s just such a pleasure.

